## 8. What the venue sources do not establish

- No venue rule gives a minimum size for text inside figures (§5 is a recommendation).
- The NeurIPS 2026 library snapshot is from 2026-11-14; if the call changes later it must be re-read. The camera-ready size limit is not stated.
- The sample in §6 is 13 papers I chose; it describes how such papers are written, it is not a statistic of the venue. The word and citation counts come from PDF text extraction and link annotations and have a few percent noise; figure and table counts come from caption lines and were spot-checked against six papers.
- A reviewer's reading of "General" versus "Negative Results" for a null finding is my reading of the Reviewer Guidelines, not a rule stated for this case.

